hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18197","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abdul-Hamid, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani narrated to us, he said: Al-Daylami narrated to us that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: We are in a cold land, and we seek help with a drink made for us from wheat. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Does it intoxicate? He said: Yes. He said: Then do not drink it. So he repeated to him a second time, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Does it intoxicate? He said: Yes. He said: Then do not drink it. He said: So he repeated to him a third time, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Does it intoxicate? He said: Yes. He said: Then do not drink it. He said: They cannot be patient without it. He said: If they cannot be patient without it, then kill them."
"18198","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Daylam al-Himyari who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a cold land, enduring therein hard labor, and we make a drink from this wheat to strengthen ourselves for our labors and for the cold of our land. He said: Does it intoxicate? I said: Yes. He said: Then avoid it. He said: Then I came from before him and said to him likewise, and he said: Does it intoxicate? I said: Yes. He said: Then avoid it. I said: The people will not abandon it. He said: If they do not abandon it, then kill them."
"18199","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abdul-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, that Daylam informed them that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a cold land, and we drink a drink to strengthen ourselves with. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Does it intoxicate? He said: Yes. He said: Then he repeated the question to him. He said: Does it intoxicate? He said: Yes. He said: Then do not approach it. He said: They will never be patient without it. He said: Whoever cannot be patient without it, then kill him."
